claim.claim-text:
a transport chamber (125A-125D) with a substrate transport opening arranged for communication with a substrate station module;
a drive section (200, 201) connected to the transport chamber, and having a motor defining at least one independent drive axis;
a robot arm (210-213) mounted inside the transport chamber, and having an end effector (210A-213E) at a distal end of the robot arm, configured to support a substrate (S) thereon, the robot arm being operably connected to the drive section generating, with the at least one independent drive axis, at least arm motion in a direction extending and retracting the robot arm and moving the end effector, in the direction, from a retracted position to an extended position;
an imaging system (500) with a camera (501) mounted in a predetermined location with respect to the transport chamber and disposed so as to image at least part of the robot arm; and
a controller (110) communicably connected to the imaging system and configured to image, with the camera, the at least part of the robot arm retracting to or in a predetermined repeatable retracted position (650, 650') defined by the at least one independent drive axis, the controller effecting capture of a first image (570) of the at least part of the robot arm on registry of the robot arm retraction proximate to or in the predetermined repeatable retracted position,
wherein the controller is configured to identify a positional variance of the at least part of the robot arm from comparison of the first image (570) with a calibration image (590) of the at least part of the robot arm, and from the positional variance determine a motion compensation distance changing the extended position of the robot arm.

providing a transport chamber (125A-125D) of a substrate transport apparatus (104), the transport chamber having a substrate transport opening arranged for communication with a substrate station module;
providing a drive section (200, 201) connected to the transport chamber, and having a motor defining at least one independent drive axis;
providing a robot arm (210-213) mounted inside the transport chamber, and having an end effector (210A-213E) at a distal end of the robot arm, configured to support a substrate (S) thereon, the robot arm being operably connected to the drive section;
generating, with the at least one independent drive axis, at least robot arm motion in a direction extending and retracting the robot arm and moving the end effector, in the direction, from a retracted position to an extended position;
imaging, with a camera (501) of an imaging system (500) mounted in a predetermined location with respect to the transport chamber, at least part of the robot arm moving to or in a predetermined repeatable retracted position (650, 650') defined by the at least one independent drive axis;
capturing, with a controller (110) communicably connected to the imaging system (500), a first image (570) of the at least part of the robot arm on registry of the robot arm proximate to or in the predetermined retracted repeatable position (650, 650') decoupled from encoder data of the at least one drive axis; and
identifying, with the controller (110), a positional variance of the at least part of the robot arm from comparison of the first image (570) with a calibration image (590) of the at least part of the robot arm, and from the positional variance determining a motion compensation distance changing the extended position of the robot arm.
